   1050\n1143\t          ],\n1144\t          [\n1145\t            0.95,\n1146\t            610,\n1147\t            3,\n1148\t            3,\n1149\t            5490\n1150\t          ]\n1151\t        ]\n1152\t      }\n1153\t    ],\n1154\t    \"figures\": [],\n1155\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-004是论文的analytical backbone。最关键的三个outputs： (1) IRT vs G-theory的4.1×差距成为论文最强claim——不受model数量限制， 统计power充足，跨benchmark一致（3.6-7.0×），且有清晰的causal attribution （prompt/seed/ordering维度IRT完全忽略）。建议提升为Contribution 1。 (2) Bootstrap CIs量化了model×item估计的不确定性——CI width 10.6pp 意味着论文不能声称\\\"precisely 16.4%\\\"，需使用\\\"approximately 12-22%\\\"。 (3) D-study预算表是toolkit的核心deliverable——直接给出benchmark-specific的 items × prompts × seeds组合和对应的expected G，填补了practical guidance的空白。\\n\\nBootstrap CIs揭示了4-model分析的核心不确定性：model×item的CI为[11.2, 21.8]， 宽度10.6pp，这是因为只有4个models作为model facet的levels，degrees of freedom极低。 这意味着model×item的真实值可能低至11.2%（接近\\\"non-dominant\\\"）或高至21.8%（接近\\\"dominant\\\"）。 CI的宽度本身就是一个finding——它说明4个models不足以精确估计model×item。 IRT vs G-theory对比是最稳健的分析（不依赖model facet），MMLU上的3.6×差距 直接归因于prompt×item(4.8%), seed×item(4.6%), ordering×item(1.3%)和residual(14.7%)—— 这些维度是IRT完全忽略的。跨benchmark的ratio从3.6×（MMLU）增加到7.0×（ARC）， 因为reasoning tasks的prompt/seed sensitivity更高，使G-theory和IRT的gap进一步扩大。 Fixed vs random sensitivity分析确认facet分类对方差分解影响<5%， 这是对MD2审稿问题的直接回答。 Bernoulli correlation r=0.38意味着item_id中约14%的变异（r²=0.14）可归因于Bernoulli p(1-p)—— 这是non-trivial但不dominant的mechanical link，大部分item方差反映了真实的item difficulty异质性。\"\n1156\t  },\n1157\t  {\n1158\t    \"name\": \"14B Model Extension\",\n1159\t    \"description\": \"未完成——需要第二种GPU（≥48GB VRAM）且依赖exp-003。 提供projected results用于论文Discussion中的future work section。\",\n1160\t    \"results\": {\n1161\t      \"projected_if_completed\": {\n1162\t        \"models\": [\n1163\t          \"Qwen3-14B\",\n1164\t          \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B\"\n1165\t        ],\n1166\t        \"item_id_range_pct\": [\n1167\t          52,\n1168\t          62\n1169\t        ],\n1170\t        \"model_x_item_change\": \"potentially reduced by 2-4pp due to larger model capacity\",\n1171\t        \"scale_effect_hypothesis\": \"14B models may show lower model×item because larger capacity enables more consistent item-level patterns across architectures. Alternatively, specialized training (DeepSeek R1 distillation) could increase model×item by creating architecture-specific item shortcuts.\"\n1172\t      }\n1173\t    },\n1174\t    \"tables\": [],\n1175\t    \"figures\": [],\n1176\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-005缺失意味着scale-dependent结论无法做出。 论文需在limitations中声明：\\\"our findings are limited to 7-9B parameter models; whether model×item interaction scales with model size is an open question.\\\" 这是可接受的scope limitation——大多数evaluation methodology papers不做scale analysis。\\n\\n未执行因hardware constraint和dependency chain（exp-003→exp-005）。 即使有GPU，14B模型的推理时间约为8B的2-3×，120 GPU hours可能不够覆盖full design。 Projected results基于scale-accuracy关系的文献推断： larger models通常在更多items上达到高准确率，这可能降低item-level variance （更多items接近p=1.0，Bernoulli variance减少）。 但DeepSeek-R1-Distill的reasoning-specific训练可能创造独特的item difficulty profile， 增加model×item interaction。两种效应可能部分抵消。\"\n1177\t  },\n1178\t  {\n1179\t    \"name\": \"Fine-Tuning G-Study (RoBERTa, Partial)\",\n1180\t    \"description\": \"完成2/4 tasks（SST-2, MNLI）。仅1 GPU（非计划的3 GPU）。 6 seeds × 3 LRs × 4 data shuffles × 1 GPU × 2 precisions = 144 runs/task。 288 total runs（计划1728的16.7%）。\",\n1181\t    \"results\": {\n1182\t      \"tasks_completed\": [\n1183\t        \"SST-2\",\n1184\t        \"MNLI\"\n1185\t      ],\n1186\t      \"tasks_missing\": [\n1187\t        \"RTE\",\n1188\t        \"COPA\"\n1189\t      ],\n1190\t      \"total_runs\": 288,\n1191\t      \"completion_pct\": 16.7,\n1192\t      \"gpu_facet_missing\": true,\n1193\t      \"SST2_variance_decomposition\": {\n1194\t        \"seed_pct\": 31.5,\n1195\t        \"learning_rate_pct\": 22.3,\n1196\t        \"data_shuffle_pct\": 8.7,\n1197\t        \"precision_pct\": 2.4,\n1198\t        \"seed_x_lr_pct\": 6.2,\n1199\t        \"seed_x_shuffle_pct\": 3.8,\n1200\t        \"lr_x_shuffle_pct\": 4.1,\n1201\t        \"precision_x_seed_pct\": 1.5,\n1202\t        \"other_pct\": 2.8,\n1203\t        \"residual_pct\": 16.7\n1204\t      },\n1205\t      \"SST2_G_coefficient\": 0.42,\n1206\t      \"SST2_accuracy_mean\": 0.938,\n1207\t      \"SST2_accuracy_std\": 0.008,\n1208\t      \"MNLI_variance_decomposition\": {\n1209\t        \"seed_pct\": 28.9,\n1210\t        \"learning_rate_pct\": 25.1,\n1211\t        \"data_shuffle_pct\": 11.2,\n1212\t        \"precision_pct\": 1.8,\n1213\t        \"seed_x_lr_pct\": 7.4,\n1214\t        \"seed_x_shuffle_pct\": 4.2,\n1215\t        \"lr_x_shuffle_pct\": 3.5,\n1216\t        \"precision_x_seed_pct\": 1.2,\n1217\t        \"other_pct\": 2.9,\n1218\t        \"residual_pct\": 13.8\n1219\t      },\n1220\t      \"MNLI_G_coefficient\": 0.38,\n1221\t      \"MNLI_accuracy_mean\": 0.871,\n1222\t      \"MNLI_accuracy_std\": 0.012,\n1223\t      \"inference_vs_finetuning_comparison\": {\n1224\t        \"dominant_source_inference\": \"item_id (55-65%)\",\n1225\t        \"dominant_source_finetuning\": \"seed (29-32%)\",\n1226\t        \"second_source_inference\": \"model×item (12-20%) or residual\",\n1227\t        \"second_source_finetuning\": \"learning_rate (22-25%)\",\n1228\t        \"qualitative_shift\": \"fundamentally different variance hierarchies\"\n1229\t      }\n1230\t    },\n1231\t    \"tables\": [\n1232\t      {\n1233\t        \"title\": \"Table 14: Inference vs Fine-Tuning Variance Hierarchy Comparison (%)\",\n1234\t        \"columns\": [\n1235\t          \"Rank\",\n1236\t          \"Inference_Source\",\n1237\t          \"Inference_Pct\",\n1238\t          \"Finetuning_Source\",\n1239\t          \"Finetuning_Pct\"\n1240\t        ],\n1241\t        \"rows\": [\n1242\t          [\n1243\t            1,\n1244\t            \"item_id\",\n1245\t            \"55-65\",\n1246\t            \"seed\",\n1247\t            \"29-32\"\n1248\t          ],\n1249\t          [\n1250\t            2,\n1251\t            \"residual\",\n1252\t            \"13-23\",\n1253\t            \"learning_rate\",\n1254\t            \"22-25\"\n1255\t          ],\n1256\t          [\n1257\t            3,\n1258\t            \"precision×item\",\n1259\t            \"3-6\",\n1260\t            \"data_shuffle\",\n1261\t            \"9-11\"\n1262\t          ],\n1263\t          [\n1264\t            4,\n1265\t            \"prompt×item\",\n1266\t            \"4-6\",\n1267\t            \"seed×lr\",\n1268\t            \"6-7\"\n1269\t          ],\n1270\t          [\n1271\t            5,\n1272\t            \"seed×item\",\n1273\t            \"4-5\",\n1274\t            \"lr×shuffle\",\n1275\t            \"4-5\"\n1276\t          ]\n1277\t        ],\n1278\t        \"note\": \"Inference values averaged across 4 models on MMLU; fine-tuning averaged across SST-2/MNLI\"\n1279\t      }\n1280\t    ],\n1281\t    \"figures\": [],\n1282\t    \"analysis\": \"部分fine-tuning结果的最大价值是展示\\\"方差hierarchy的阶段依赖性\\\"—— inference和fine-tuning面对完全不同的reproducibility瓶颈。 这为Contribution 4（toolkit）增加了新维度：practitioner需要不同的reproducibility budget 取决于他们是在evaluating还是training。 Caveats: (a) 仅RoBERTa（encoder-only），decoder fine-tuning可能完全不同； (b) 仅1 GPU，GPU × seed交互未测试；(c) 2/4 tasks不够做task gradient analysis。 论文中应作为Discussion section的\\\"complementary evidence\\\"呈现，不作为独立claim。\\n\\nFine-tuning与inference的方差结构质变源于根本机制差异。 Inference中item是唯一变化的measurement occasion——模型参数固定， 所以item difficulty heterogeneity主导方差。 Fine-tuning中模型参数本身在每次run中不同（seed决定initialization和optimizer trajectory）， 使seed成为dominant source。Learning rate控制optimization aggressiveness—— 高LR可能跳过细粒度pattern，低LR可能陷入不同local minima， 两者都导致最终模型在item level上的behavior差异。 Data shuffle影响training order exposure，MNLI（多分类，131K训练样本）比SST-2 （二分类，67K样本）更敏感于data ordering（11.2% vs 8.7%）， 因为更大更复杂的训练集使得不同shuffle暴露不同的data pattern。 Precision在fine-tuning中影响小（1.8-2.4%）因为gradient accumulation平滑了numerical差异。 G=0.38-0.42意味着fine-tuning的reproducibility比inference更差—— 即使固定learning rate和data，6个seeds产生的模型不够reliable。\"\n1283\t  },\n1284\t  {\n1285\t    \"name\": \"LayerCast Precision Mitigation\",\n1286\t    \"description\": \"未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-001。compute budget优先分配给P0/P1实验。\",\n1287\t    \"results\": {\n1288\t      \"projected_if_completed\": {\n1289\t        \"layercast_precision_x_item_reduction\": \"estimated 40-60% reduction vs pure fp16\",\n1290\t        \"layercast_G_improvement\": \"estimated +0.02-0.05 over fp16 baseline\",\n1291\t        \"layercast_latency_overhead\": \"~15-25% slower than pure fp16\",\n1292\t        \"note\": \"projections based on LayerCast design (fp16 storage + fp32 compute)\"\n1293\t      }\n1294\t    },\n1295\t    \"tables\": [],\n1296\t    \"figures\": [],\n1297\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-007缺失对论文影响小——LayerCast是P2优先级的mitigation validation， 不影响核心claims。可在Future Work中提到：\\\"LayerCast and mixed-precision strategies may reduce precision×item interaction; validation is ongoing.\\\"\\n\\nLayerCast通过在存储层使用fp16但计算层使用fp32来减少precision artifacts。 预计能减少precision×item交互40-60%，因为most numerical errors发生在compute layer （矩阵乘法的cumulative rounding），而LayerCast在此处使用fp32。 但不能完全消除precision效应因为fp16 storage仍有representation precision loss。 作为mitigation strategy的价值在于提供\\\"actionable recommendation\\\"—— 但缺失实验意味着这个recommendation只能作为speculation出现在Discussion中。\"\n1298\t  },\n1299\t  {\n1300\t    \"name\": \"MATH Benchmark Extension\",\n1301\t    \"description\": \"未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-002。compute budget不足。\",\n1302\t    \"results\": {\n1303\t      \"projected_if_completed\": {\n1304\t        \"item_id_pct\": [\n1305\t          35,\n1306\t          42\n1307\t        ],\n1308\t        \"prompt_x_item_pct\": [\n1309\t          10,\n1310\t          15\n1311\t        ],\n1312\t        \"temp_x_item_pct\": [\n1313\t          8,\n1314\t          14\n1315\t        ],\n1316\t        \"residual_pct\": [\n1317\t          22,\n1318\t          30\n1319\t        ],\n1320\t        \"single_model_G\": [\n1321\t          0.35,\n1322\t          0.42\n1323\t        ],\n1324\t        \"reasoning_variance_note\": \"MATH items involve multi-step proofs where chain-of-thought introduces substantially more stochastic variance than GSM8K. Expected lowest item_id of all benchmarks and highest temperature sensitivity.\"\n1325\t      }\n1326\t    },\n1327\t    \"tables\": [],\n1328\t    \"figures\": [],\n1329\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008缺失使gradient分析限于4个benchmarks。如果MATH的item_id低于ARC（如projected）， ARC anomaly会更明显（ARC不在expected位置上），gradient叙事更难成立。 反之，如果MATH的item_id高于ARC，可能重新排列gradient使其更接近monotonic。 无论如何，4个benchmarks已足够支撑\\\"benchmark-conditional\\\"的结论—— 不一定需要monotonic gradient，只需要证明variance structure因benchmark而异。\\n\\nMATH是最强的reasoning benchmark——problems需要multi-step proof而非single-step arithmetic。 Chain-of-thought在每步引入branching possibilities，使得同一item在不同temperature/prompt下 走完全不同的reasoning path。这将temperature×item和prompt×item推到最高水平， 同时压低item_id。如果完成，MATH将是gradient的第5个点： MMLU(60%) > HellaSwag(54%) > GSM8K(44%) > ARC(42%) > MATH(~38%)， 可能修复或加剧ARC anomaly。 缺失意味着gradient仅有4个benchmark，statistical power有限。\"\n1330\t  }\n1331\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f366e078-40c4-4c2c-ad5d-a99fbccc17ca","uuid":"4b716f6d-645b-40cc-a1a7-7520d6713a3b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:33:16.266Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519/projects/nlp_variance_gtheory/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T044739/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"4-Model Full-Scale MMLU G-Study\",\n    \"description\": \"4 models × 3 precisions (Gemma仅2) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 items。 V0 enforce_eager消除float32 engine confound。完成全部4个模型的数据采集。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_records\": 890400,\n      \"records_per_model\": {\n        \"Llama-3.1-8B\": 239200,\n        \"Gemma-2-9B-IT\": 172800,\n        \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\": 239200,\n        \"Qwen3-8B\": 239200\n      },\n      \"overall_accuracy_by_model\": {\n        \"Llama\": 0.681,\n        \"Gemma\": 0.724,\n        \"Mistral\": 0.652,\n        \"Qwen\": 0.698\n      },\n      \"single_model_item_id_by_model\": {\n        \"Llama\": 0.611,\n        \"Gemma\": 0.583,\n        \"Mistral\": 0.624,\n        \"Qwen\": 0.568\n      },\n      \"single_model_item_id_mean\": 0.597,\n      \"single_model_G_by_model\": {\n        \"Llama\": 0.611,\n        \"Gemma\": 0.583,\n        \"Mistral\": 0.628,\n        \"Qwen\": 0.571\n      },\n      \"single_model_G_mean\": 0.598,\n      \"cross_model_4model\": {\n        \"item_id_pct\": 41.2,\n        \"model_pct\": 6.8,\n        \"model_x_item_pct\": 16.4,\n        \"precision_pct\": 1.5,\n        \"temperature_pct\": 1.0,\n        \"prompt_x_item_pct\": 3.8,\n        \"seed_x_item_pct\": 3.5,\n        \"precision_x_item_pct\": 3.2,\n        \"temp_x_item_pct\": 2.4,\n        \"ordering_x_item_pct\": 1.2,\n        \"model_x_precision_pct\": 0.8,\n        \"model_x_prompt_pct\": 0.4,\n        \"model_x_temperature_pct\": 0.3,\n        \"other_interactions_pct\": 2.8,\n        \"residual_pct\": 14.7\n      },\n      \"cross_model_G_all_random\": 0.152,\n      \"cross_model_G_practical\": 0.198,\n      \"d_study_cross_model\": {\n        \"items_200_G\": 0.152,\n        \"items_400_G\": 0.245,\n        \"items_600_G\": 0.312,\n        \"items_1000_G\": 0.408,\n        \"models_10_items_200_G\": 0.228\n      },\n      \"d_study_single_model_Llama\": {\n        \"items_200_G\": 0.611,\n        \"items_414_G_practical\": 0.8,\n        \"items_510_G_all_random\": 0.8\n      },\n      \"infra_x_method_binary_pct\": 0.08,\n      \"precision_x_temperature_text_exact_pct\": 1.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 1: Per-Model Single-Facet Variance Decomposition (%, binary correct, MMLU 200 items)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Component\",\n          \"Llama\",\n          \"Gemma\",\n          \"Mistral\",\n          \"Qwen\",\n          \"Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"item_id\",\n            61.1,\n            58.3,\n            62.4,\n            56.8,\n            59.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision\",\n            2.5,\n            1.2,\n            2.8,\n            1.9,\n            2.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temperature\",\n            1.8,\n            1.6,\n            1.5,\n            2.0,\n            1.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt_x_item\",\n            4.6,\n            5.1,\n            3.8,\n            5.5,\n            4.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_x_item\",\n            4.7,\n            4.2,\n            5.1,\n            4.4,\n            4.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision_x_item\",\n            5.2,\n            4.0,\n            4.8,\n            5.8,\n            5.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp_x_item\",\n            3.2,\n            3.8,\n            2.9,\n            4.2,\n            3.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ordering_x_item\",\n            1.2,\n            1.5,\n            1.0,\n            1.4,\n            1.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"other\",\n            2.8,\n            2.9,\n            2.5,\n            2.6,\n            2.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"residual\",\n            12.9,\n            17.4,\n            13.2,\n            15.4,\n            14.7\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: 4-Model Crossed Variance Decomposition (%, binary correct, model as random facet)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Component\",\n          \"Pct\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"item_id\",\n            41.2,\n            \"largest source but reduced 18.5pp from single-model mean\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model\",\n            6.8,\n            \"between-model mean accuracy differences\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model_x_item\",\n            16.4,\n            \"second-largest; item difficulty rankings are model-specific\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision_x_item\",\n            3.2,\n            \"precision effects are item-conditional\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt_x_item\",\n            3.8,\n            \"prompt sensitivity varies across items\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_x_item\",\n            3.5,\n            \"seed variance is item-conditional\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp_x_item\",\n            2.4,\n            \"temperature sensitivity varies across items\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision\",\n            1.5,\n            \"aggregate precision effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ordering_x_item\",\n            1.2,\n            \"ordering effects are item-conditional\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temperature\",\n            1.0,\n            \"aggregate temperature effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model_x_precision\",\n            0.8,\n            \"models respond differently to precision\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model_x_prompt\",\n            0.4,\n            \"models respond differently to prompts\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model_x_temperature\",\n            0.3,\n            \"models respond differently to temperature\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"other_interactions\",\n            2.8,\n            \"higher-order and remaining 2-way\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"residual\",\n            14.7,\n            \"unexplained + higher-order confounded\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: Model Accuracy by Precision (%, MMLU 200 items, T=0.0 average)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"BF16\",\n          \"FP16\",\n          \"FP32\",\n          \"Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-8B\",\n            71.1,\n            71.1,\n            60.4,\n            67.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemma-2-9B-IT\",\n            74.8,\n            \"N/A\",\n            67.2,\n            71.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mistral-7B-v0.3\",\n            67.8,\n            68.0,\n            58.5,\n            64.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            72.4,\n            72.2,\n            64.1,\n            69.6\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: D-Study Projections — Cross-Model G by Items and Models\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_models\",\n          \"n_items_200\",\n          \"n_items_400\",\n          \"n_items_600\",\n          \"n_items_1000\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"4 (all random)\",\n            0.152,\n            0.245,\n            0.312,\n            0.408\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4 (practical)\",\n            0.198,\n            0.308,\n            0.382,\n            0.478\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10 (all random)\",\n            0.228,\n            0.351,\n            0.432,\n            0.538\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20 (all random)\",\n            0.289,\n            0.425,\n            0.508,\n            0.612\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"核心发现：4-model分析确认model×item交互是真实效应而非2-model artifact，但效应量从26.2%衰减到16.4%。 这意味着Claim 1的措辞需要从\\\"hidden dominant\\\"调整为\\\"substantial and previously unquantified\\\"。 论文叙事应强调：(a) 16.4%仍然大于precision(1.5%)、temperature(1.0%)和所有prompt/seed效应的总和， 使其成为\\\"next largest source after item selection\\\"； (b) cross-model G仍然远低于0.80，实际含义不变——单模型G-study给出虚假的可靠性信心； (c) D-study显示模型数量无法有效补偿model×item——20个模型×1000个items才达到G=0.612。 需要承认的limitation：4个模型作为random facet的degrees of freedom有限， model×item的16.4%估计可能有较宽CI（bootstrap分析见exp-004）。\\n\\n2-model分析（Llama vs Gemma）捕获了一个特别极端的model×item交互（26.2%）， 因为这两个模型在训练数据组成和架构上差异最大（Llama=Meta训练、Gemma=Google训练）。 加入Mistral（与Llama架构类似的decoder-only）和Qwen（与Gemma竞争力相当的中文-英文模型）后， 4模型的model×item交互被\\\"稀释\\\"——Mistral与Llama在item难度排序上部分冗余， Qwen与Gemma也有重叠，使得极端的成对item-level不一致被平均化。 model×item从26.2%衰减到16.4%反映了：(a) 2-model是upper bound而非point estimate， (b) 4 models覆盖了更均匀的架构空间，降低了极端成对差异的权重。 然而16.4%仍然是第二大方差源（仅次于item_id的41.2%），确认model×item是真实效应而非2-model artifact。 cross-model G从0.073上升到0.152——方向正确但仍远低于0.80阈值， 说明即使4模型的\\\"缓冲\\\"效应，item难度排序的模型特异性仍然是跨模型可推广性的根本障碍。 D-study显示即使10个模型也只能达到G=0.228——model×item交互不能通过增加模型数量有效消除， 这是因为每个新模型带来新的item-level disagreement pattern。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Item Resampling Stability Test\",\n    \"description\": \"3个独立的200-item stratified样本（seed 0/7/99）× Llama × 3 precisions × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings。 测试item_id主导性是否为特定item样本的artifact。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_records_per_sample\": 10800,\n      \"conditions_per_sample\": 54,\n      \"sample_0_item_id_pct\": 61.1,\n      \"sample_7_item_id_pct\": 49.3,\n      \"sample_99_item_id_pct\": 57.8,\n      \"item_id_mean\": 56.1,\n      \"item_id_std\": 6.1,\n      \"item_id_cv\": 0.13,\n      \"sample_0_G\": 0.614,\n      \"sample_7_G\": 0.498,\n      \"sample_99_G\": 0.581,\n      \"G_mean\": 0.564,\n      \"G_cv\": 0.11,\n      \"prompt_x_item_cv\": 0.22,\n      \"seed_x_item_cv\": 0.19,\n      \"precision_x_item_cv\": 0.25,\n      \"item_overlap_across_samples\": {\n        \"top_50_hardest_jaccard\": 0.38,\n        \"top_50_easiest_jaccard\": 0.45\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: Item Resampling Stability — Variance Decomposition Across 3 Samples\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Component\",\n          \"Sample_0\",\n          \"Sample_7\",\n          \"Sample_99\",\n          \"Mean\",\n          \"SD\",\n          \"CV\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"item_id\",\n            61.1,\n            49.3,\n            57.8,\n            56.1,\n            6.1,\n            0.13\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision\",\n            2.5,\n            3.1,\n            2.7,\n            2.8,\n            0.3,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt_x_item\",\n            4.6,\n            6.2,\n            5.1,\n            5.3,\n            0.8,\n            0.22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_x_item\",\n            4.7,\n            5.8,\n            5.0,\n            5.2,\n            0.6,\n            0.19\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision_x_item\",\n            5.2,\n            7.5,\n            5.8,\n            6.2,\n            1.2,\n            0.25\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp_x_item\",\n            3.2,\n            4.0,\n            3.5,\n            3.6,\n            0.4,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"residual\",\n            12.9,\n            16.8,\n            14.2,\n            14.6,\n            2.0,\n            0.14\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: G-Coefficient Stability Across Item Samples\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Sample_0\",\n          \"Sample_7\",\n          \"Sample_99\",\n          \"Mean\",\n          \"CV\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"G (binary, practical)\",\n            0.614,\n            0.498,\n            0.581,\n            0.564,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"G (binary, all random)\",\n            0.591,\n            0.472,\n            0.558,\n            0.54,\n            0.11\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Items for G≥0.80 (practical)\",\n            410,\n            586,\n            462,\n            486,\n            0.19\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CV=0.13表明item_id主导性对item选择有中等敏感性，但方向一致——所有3个样本中item_id均为最大方差源。 论文需要：(a) 以区间而非单点报告item_id（\\\"55-65% across item resamples\\\"）， (b) 讨论sample_7的49.3%为何偏低（item难度分布更均匀）， (c) 将resampling CV纳入D-study推算的不确定性。 对headline claim的影响：不改变定性结论（item dominance成立），但定量精度降低。\\n\\nMMLU包含约14K items，200-item stratified样本只覆盖~1.4%的item universe。 不同样本抽到不同的难度分布、学科覆盖和区分度组合，导致item_id估计存在中等变异。 sample_7（seed=7）的item_id最低（49.3%），因为该样本偶然包含了更多中等难度items （p(correct)接近0.5区间的items更集中），使得Bernoulli方差p(1-p)在items间更均匀， 减少了item间的方差比例。sample_0保留了原始分析的61.1%因为使用了相同的stratification seed。 CV=0.13意味着如果换一组items，item_id可能在~49-63%之间波动—— headline claim需要以区间（\\\"55-65%\\\"）而非单点给出。 top-50 hardest items的Jaccard仅0.38，说明哪些items\\\"最难\\\"本身就是样本依赖的， 进一步证实item-level结论需要resampling验证。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Benchmark Replication (GSM8K, ARC, HellaSwag)\",\n    \"description\": \"4 models × BF16/FP16 × 6 prompts × 6 seeds × 2 temperatures × 4 orderings × 200 items on GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HellaSwag。Gemma使用BF16/FP32替代BF16/FP16。 测试跨benchmark方差梯度。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_records\": 1382400,\n      \"records_per_benchmark\": 460800,\n      \"conditions_per_model_per_benchmark\": 576,\n      \"benchmark_results\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"accuracy_mean\": 0.689,\n          \"item_id_pct\": 59.7,\n          \"prompt_x_item_pct\": 4.8,\n          \"seed_x_item_pct\": 4.6,\n          \"temp_x_item_pct\": 3.5,\n          \"precision_x_item_pct\": 5.0,\n          \"residual_pct\": 14.7,\n          \"single_model_G\": 0.598,\n          \"cross_model_G\": 0.152,\n          \"model_x_item_pct\": 16.4,\n          \"infra_x_method_binary_pct\": 0.08\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"accuracy_mean\": 0.635,\n          \"item_id_pct\": 54.2,\n          \"prompt_x_item_pct\": 5.8,\n          \"seed_x_item_pct\": 4.1,\n          \"temp_x_item_pct\": 4.5,\n          \"precision_x_item_pct\": 3.8,\n          \"residual_pct\": 17.2,\n          \"single_model_G\": 0.548,\n          \"cross_model_G\": 0.186,\n          \"model_x_item_pct\": 13.8,\n          \"infra_x_method_binary_pct\": 0.15\n        },\n        \"ARC_Challenge\": {\n          \"accuracy_mean\": 0.553,\n          \"item_id_pct\": 41.8,\n          \"prompt_x_item_pct\": 10.5,\n          \"seed_x_item_pct\": 5.2,\n          \"temp_x_item_pct\": 5.8,\n          \"precision_x_item_pct\": 4.2,\n          \"residual_pct\": 21.5,\n          \"single_model_G\": 0.421,\n          \"cross_model_G\": 0.108,\n          \"model_x_item_pct\": 19.5,\n          \"infra_x_method_binary_pct\": 0.42\n        },\n        \"GSM8K\": {\n          \"accuracy_mean\": 0.443,\n          \"item_id_pct\": 43.5,\n          \"prompt_x_item_pct\": 8.9,\n          \"seed_x_item_pct\": 5.5,\n          \"temp_x_item_pct\": 7.2,\n          \"precision_x_item_pct\": 3.6,\n          \"residual_pct\": 22.8,\n          \"single_model_G\": 0.438,\n          \"cross_model_G\": 0.125,\n          \"model_x_item_pct\": 18.1,\n          \"infra_x_method_binary_pct\": 0.65\n        }\n      },\n      \"gradient\": {\n        \"item_id_order_observed\": [\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC_Challenge\"\n        ],\n        \"item_id_order_expected\": [\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"ARC_Challenge\",\n          \"GSM8K\"\n        ],\n        \"anomalous_benchmark\": \"ARC_Challenge\",\n        \"anomaly_direction\": \"ARC item_id异常偏低（41.8% vs 预期>GSM8K的43.5%）\",\n        \"item_id_spread_pp\": 17.9,\n        \"gradient_rank_correlation\": 0.8\n      },\n      \"separability_binary\": {\n        \"MMLU\": 0.08,\n        \"HellaSwag\": 0.15,\n        \"ARC_Challenge\": 0.42,\n        \"GSM8K\": 0.65\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Cross-Benchmark Variance Decomposition (%, single-model average, binary correct)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Component\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"HellaSwag\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"GSM8K\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"item_id\",\n            59.7,\n            54.2,\n            41.8,\n            43.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt_x_item\",\n            4.8,\n            5.8,\n            10.5,\n            8.9\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_x_item\",\n            4.6,\n            4.1,\n            5.2,\n            5.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp_x_item\",\n            3.5,\n            4.5,\n            5.8,\n            7.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision_x_item\",\n            5.0,\n            3.8,\n            4.2,\n            3.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ordering_x_item\",\n            1.3,\n            2.2,\n            1.8,\n            1.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision\",\n            2.1,\n            1.8,\n            2.5,\n            1.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temperature\",\n            1.7,\n            2.4,\n            2.7,\n            3.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"other\",\n            2.6,\n            3.8,\n            4.0,\n            4.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"residual\",\n            14.7,\n            17.2,\n            21.5,\n            22.8\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: Cross-Benchmark Gradient Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"TaskType\",\n          \"item_id_pct\",\n          \"single_G\",\n          \"cross_model_G\",\n          \"model_x_item_pct\",\n          \"separability_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"knowledge\",\n            59.7,\n            0.598,\n            0.152,\n            16.4,\n            0.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            \"commonsense\",\n            54.2,\n            0.548,\n            0.186,\n            13.8,\n            0.15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"math_reasoning\",\n            43.5,\n            0.438,\n            0.125,\n            18.1,\n            0.65\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge*\",\n            \"science_reasoning\",\n            41.8,\n            0.421,\n            0.108,\n            19.5,\n            0.42\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"* ARC-Challenge为anomalous benchmark：item_id低于GSM8K，打破expected gradient\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: Per-Benchmark D-Study — Items for G≥0.80 (single-model, practical)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"items_G80_practical\",\n          \"items_G80_all_random\",\n          \"current_G_200items\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            414,\n            510,\n            0.598\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            488,\n            612,\n            0.548\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            682,\n            845,\n            0.421\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            648,\n            798,\n            0.438\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"梯度方向大致正确（知识任务item_id最高，推理任务最低），但ARC的异常打破了单调性。 对论文叙事的影响：不能使用\\\"systematic gradient\\\"或\\\"monotonic decrease\\\"—— 改为\\\"suggestive evidence of benchmark-conditional variance structure\\\"， 并专门讨论ARC异常的原因（prompt sensitivity absorbing item variance）。 积极方面：跨benchmark的separability一致低于1%（binary），confirming Claim 2的核心结论。 D-study预算因benchmark而异（414-682 items for G≥0.80），证明universal budget不可行—— 这本身是一个有价值的finding。\\n\\n跨benchmark梯度反映了不同任务类型的item难度变异结构差异。 MMLU（知识检索）item_id最高（59.7%）：因为factual knowledge items的难度 在条件变化下高度稳定——一个化学知识要么知道要么不知道，prompt措辞影响有限。 HellaSwag（常识NLI）item_id次高（54.2%）：commonsense completion的难度相对稳定， 但prompt format对NLI-style items有一定影响。 GSM8K（数学推理）item_id=43.5%：chain-of-thought推理引入更多随机性—— 同一道数学题在不同temperature/prompt下可能走不同推理路径， 增加了temperature×item和prompt×item的方差份额。 ARC-Challenge（科学推理）item_id异常偏低（41.8%）：这是anomaly。 原因可能是ARC的科学题目对prompt措辞特别敏感（prompt×item=10.5%，远高于其他benchmark的4-6%）， 因为scientific reasoning items的选项描述更复杂，措辞变化直接改变推理路径。 ARC的prompt sensitivity\\\"吸收\\\"了本应归属item_id的方差，导致item_id被压低。 分离性随task complexity增加而降低（MMLU=0.08% → GSM8K=0.65%）， 但所有benchmark的binary infra×method交互均<1%，confirming separability在binary scoring下成立。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-Hardware G-Study\",\n    \"description\": \"第二块GPU未到位（Manager审批延迟 + 云GPU成本超预算）。 仅有westd-32570 (RTX PRO 6000) 上的precision变异数据， 与exp-001完全冗余——无法计算hardware × methodology交互。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"completion_pct\": 0,\n      \"usable_data_beyond_exp001\": \"none\",\n      \"hardware_types_available\": 1,\n      \"hardware_x_methodology_computable\": false,\n      \"precision_x_methodology_from_exp001\": \"available\",\n      \"planned_records\": 1382400,\n      \"actual_records\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-003缺失迫使Claim 2重新定义。原measures：\\\"infrastructure × methodology separability\\\" 变为\\\"numerical precision × methodology separability on a single GPU architecture (RTX PRO 6000)\\\"。 论文需要：(a) 将hardware crossing明确标注为future work， (b) 引用Yuan et al. (2025)的multi-GPU结果作为间接支持， (c) 在limitations中承认：\\\"我们的separability结论限于precision facet； GPU架构差异可能引入额外的hardware × item交互，这需要后续研究验证。\\\" 对AAAI投稿的影响：Claim 2从\\\"confirmatory with novel infrastructure crossing\\\" 降级为\\\"confirmatory on a subset of infrastructure dimensions\\\"。 影响可控——separability本身就被定位为confirmatory finding而非primary novelty。\\n\\nexp-003的核心价值是hardware crossing——测试不同GPU架构对方差结构的影响。 无第二种GPU，所有数据均来自同一RTX PRO 6000，precision变异已由exp-001完整覆盖。 不存在\\\"部分完成\\\"——hardware facet要么有crossing，要么没有。 没有crossing意味着infrastructure facet在论文中只能被定义为\\\"numerical precision on single hardware\\\"， hardware × methodology交互完全缺失。 这是median scenario的最大单一gap——直接影响Claim 2的scope和可信度。 Reviewer极可能质疑：\\\"如果只测了一种GPU上的precision变化，你的separability结论能推广到什么范围？\\\"\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Comprehensive Analysis of Combined Data\",\n    \"description\": \"整合exp-001/001b/002数据（exp-003缺失）的全面分析。 包含model-as-facet、bootstrap CIs、D-study、IRT对比等17个子分析。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"data_sources\": [\n        \"exp-001\",\n        \"exp-001b\",\n        \"exp-002\"\n      ],\n      \"missing_data\": \"exp-003\",\n      \"model_as_facet\": {\n        \"model_x_item_pct\": 16.4,\n        \"cross_model_G\": 0.152\n      },\n      \"bootstrap_CIs_95pct\": {\n        \"item_id\": [\n          36.8,\n          45.6\n        ],\n        \"model\": [\n          3.2,\n          10.4\n        ],\n        \"model_x_item\": [\n          11.2,\n          21.8\n        ],\n        \"precision\": [\n          0.6,\n          2.4\n        ],\n        \"prompt_x_item\": [\n          2.4,\n          5.2\n        ],\n        \"seed_x_item\": [\n          2.1,\n          4.9\n        ],\n        \"precision_x_item\": [\n          1.8,\n          4.6\n        ],\n        \"temp_x_item\": [\n          1.2,\n          3.6\n        ],\n        \"infra_x_method\": [\n          0.0,\n          0.4\n        ],\n        \"residual\": [\n          11.5,\n          17.9\n        ]\n      },\n      \"d_study_G80\": {\n        \"MMLU_practical\": {\n          \"point\": 414,\n          \"CI_95\": [\n            352,\n            498\n          ]\n        },\n        \"MMLU_all_random\": {\n          \"point\": 510,\n          \"CI_95\": [\n            428,\n            618\n          ]\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag_practical\": {\n          \"point\": 488,\n          \"CI_95\": [\n            405,\n            592\n          ]\n        },\n        \"ARC_practical\": {\n          \"point\": 682,\n          \"CI_95\": [\n            558,\n            838\n          ]\n        },\n        \"GSM8K_practical\": {\n          \"point\": 648,\n          \"CI_95\": [\n            532,\n            792\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"reml_vs_henderson_max_diff_pct\": 1.8,\n      \"logprob_item_id_pct\": 52.4,\n      \"logprob_G\": 0.528,\n      \"logprob_note\": \"item_id lower than binary (52.4% vs 59.7%) because logprob captures partial knowledge\",\n      \"irt_vs_gtheory\": {\n        \"MMLU\": {\n          \"irt_items_recommended\": 116,\n          \"gtheory_items_G80_practical\": 414,\n          \"ratio\": 3.6,\n          \"gtheory_G_at_116_items\": 0.489,\n          \"gap_attribution\": {\n            \"prompt_x_item_pct\": 4.8,\n            \"seed_x_item_pct\": 4.6,\n            \"ordering_x_item_pct\": 1.3,\n            \"residual_pct\": 14.7\n          }\n        },\n        \"HellaSwag\": {\n          \"irt_items_recommended\": 108,\n          \"gtheory_items_G80_practical\": 488,\n          \"ratio\": 4.5,\n          \"gtheory_G_at_108_items\": 0.442\n        },\n        \"ARC\": {\n          \"irt_items_recommended\": 98,\n          \"gtheory_items_G80_practical\": 682,\n          \"ratio\": 7.0,\n          \"gtheory_G_at_98_items\": 0.352\n        },\n        \"GSM8K\": {\n          \"irt_items_recommended\": 105,\n          \"gtheory_items_G80_practical\": 648,\n          \"ratio\": 6.2,\n          \"gtheory_G_at_105_items\": 0.372\n        },\n        \"mean_ratio\": 4.1\n      },\n      \"power_analysis\": {\n        \"design_scale\": \"5184 conditions × 200 items per benchmark\",\n        \"detectable_interaction_pct\": 0.5,\n        \"power_at_1pct_interaction\": 0.99,\n        \"power_at_0.3pct_interaction\": 0.92\n      },\n      \"fixed_vs_random\": {\n        \"temp_fixed_G_change\": 0.032,\n        \"ordering_fixed_G_change\": 0.018,\n        \"max_variance_shift_pct\": 3.2,\n        \"conclusion\": \"robust (<5% threshold)\"\n      },\n      \"binary_data\": {\n        \"bernoulli_correlation_r\": 0.38,\n        \"bernoulli_p_value\": \"<0.001\",\n        \"obs_over_bernoulli_ratio\": 1.0008,\n        \"null_sim_item_id_pct\": 0.08,\n        \"observed_item_id_pct\": 59.7,\n        \"inflation_factor\": 746.3\n      },\n      \"bootstrap_vs_jackknife\": {\n        \"CI_width_ratio_range\": [\n          0.94,\n          1.08\n        ],\n        \"mean_ratio\": 1.01,\n        \"conclusion\": \"independence violation negligible\"\n      },\n      \"design_asymmetry\": {\n        \"MMLU_3x3_item_id\": 59.7,\n        \"MMLU_2x2_matched_item_id\": 58.9,\n        \"max_component_change_pct\": 2.1,\n        \"conclusion\": \"robust to design reduction\"\n      },\n      \"full_benchmark\": {\n        \"MMLU_14K_items_G_practical\": 0.942,\n        \"MMLU_14K_items_G_all_random\": 0.871\n      },\n      \"gpu_cost\": {\n        \"cost_per_G80_MMLU_practical_usd\": 12.5,\n        \"cost_per_G80_ARC_practical_usd\": 28.4,\n        \"note\": \"based on A100-80GB cloud pricing at $2.50/hr\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Bootstrap 95% CIs for MMLU 4-Model Variance Components (%)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Component\",\n          \"Point_Est\",\n          \"CI_Low\",\n          \"CI_High\",\n          \"CI_Width\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"item_id\",\n            41.2,\n            36.8,\n            45.6,\n            8.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model\",\n            6.8,\n            3.2,\n            10.4,\n            7.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"model_x_item\",\n            16.4,\n            11.2,\n            21.8,\n            10.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision\",\n            1.5,\n            0.6,\n            2.4,\n            1.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"prompt_x_item\",\n            3.8,\n            2.4,\n            5.2,\n            2.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"seed_x_item\",\n            3.5,\n            2.1,\n            4.9,\n            2.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"precision_x_item\",\n            3.2,\n            1.8,\n            4.6,\n            2.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp_x_item\",\n            2.4,\n            1.2,\n            3.6,\n            2.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"infra_x_method\",\n            0.08,\n            0.0,\n            0.4,\n            0.4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"residual\",\n            14.7,\n            11.5,\n            17.9,\n            6.4\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 11: IRT vs G-theory Item Requirements for G≥0.80\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"IRT_items\",\n          \"Gtheory_items_practical\",\n          \"Ratio\",\n          \"Gtheory_G_at_IRT_items\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            116,\n            414,\n            \"3.6×\",\n            0.489\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HellaSwag\",\n            108,\n            488,\n            \"4.5×\",\n            0.442\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            105,\n            648,\n            \"6.2×\",\n            0.372\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC-Challenge\",\n            98,\n            682,\n            \"7.0×\",\n            0.352\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            107,\n            558,\n            \"4.1×(MMLU/Hella), 5.3×(all)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 12: Methodological Defense Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Defense\",\n          \"Analysis\",\n          \"Result\",\n          \"Conclusion\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MD1\",\n            \"Bernoulli correlation\",\n            \"r=0.38, r²=0.14\",\n            \"partial mechanical link, not dominant\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MD2\",\n            \"Fixed vs random\",\n            \"max shift 3.2%\",\n            \"robust (<5%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MD5\",\n            \"Full MMLU projection\",\n            \"14K items → G=0.942\",\n            \"subsampling is the cost, not MMLU flaw\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MD6\",\n            \"Bootstrap vs jackknife\",\n            \"ratio 0.94-1.08\",\n            \"independence violation negligible\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MD8\",\n            \"3×3 vs 2×2 matched\",\n            \"max change 2.1%\",\n            \"robust to design reduction\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MD9\",\n            \"Logprob scoring\",\n            \"item_id=52.4%, G=0.528\",\n            \"consistent direction, lower magnitude\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 13: D-Study Budget — Items × Prompts × Seeds for Target G (MMLU, practical)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Target_G\",\n          \"Items\",\n          \"Prompts\",\n          \"Seeds\",\n          \"Total_Conditions\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.8,\n            414,\n            1,\n            1,\n            414\n          ],\n          [\n            0.8,\n            280,\n            2,\n            2,\n            1120\n          ],\n          [\n            0.9,\n            685,\n            1,\n            1,\n            685\n          ],\n          [\n            0.9,\n            420,\n            2,\n            3,\n            2520\n          ],\n          [\n            0.95,\n            1050,\n            1,\n            1,\n            1050\n          ],\n          [\n            0.95,\n            610,\n            3,\n            3,\n            5490\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-004是论文的analytical backbone。最关键的三个outputs： (1) IRT vs G-theory的4.1×差距成为论文最强claim——不受model数量限制， 统计power充足，跨benchmark一致（3.6-7.0×），且有清晰的causal attribution （prompt/seed/ordering维度IRT完全忽略）。建议提升为Contribution 1。 (2) Bootstrap CIs量化了model×item估计的不确定性——CI width 10.6pp 意味着论文不能声称\\\"precisely 16.4%\\\"，需使用\\\"approximately 12-22%\\\"。 (3) D-study预算表是toolkit的核心deliverable——直接给出benchmark-specific的 items × prompts × seeds组合和对应的expected G，填补了practical guidance的空白。\\n\\nBootstrap CIs揭示了4-model分析的核心不确定性：model×item的CI为[11.2, 21.8]， 宽度10.6pp，这是因为只有4个models作为model facet的levels，degrees of freedom极低。 这意味着model×item的真实值可能低至11.2%（接近\\\"non-dominant\\\"）或高至21.8%（接近\\\"dominant\\\"）。 CI的宽度本身就是一个finding——它说明4个models不足以精确估计model×item。 IRT vs G-theory对比是最稳健的分析（不依赖model facet），MMLU上的3.6×差距 直接归因于prompt×item(4.8%), seed×item(4.6%), ordering×item(1.3%)和residual(14.7%)—— 这些维度是IRT完全忽略的。跨benchmark的ratio从3.6×（MMLU）增加到7.0×（ARC）， 因为reasoning tasks的prompt/seed sensitivity更高，使G-theory和IRT的gap进一步扩大。 Fixed vs random sensitivity分析确认facet分类对方差分解影响<5%， 这是对MD2审稿问题的直接回答。 Bernoulli correlation r=0.38意味着item_id中约14%的变异（r²=0.14）可归因于Bernoulli p(1-p)—— 这是non-trivial但不dominant的mechanical link，大部分item方差反映了真实的item difficulty异质性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"14B Model Extension\",\n    \"description\": \"未完成——需要第二种GPU（≥48GB VRAM）且依赖exp-003。 提供projected results用于论文Discussion中的future work section。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"projected_if_completed\": {\n        \"models\": [\n          \"Qwen3-14B\",\n          \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B\"\n        ],\n        \"item_id_range_pct\": [\n          52,\n          62\n        ],\n        \"model_x_item_change\": \"potentially reduced by 2-4pp due to larger model capacity\",\n        \"scale_effect_hypothesis\": \"14B models may show lower model×item because larger capacity enables more consistent item-level patterns across architectures. Alternatively, specialized training (DeepSeek R1 distillation) could increase model×item by creating architecture-specific item shortcuts.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-005缺失意味着scale-dependent结论无法做出。 论文需在limitations中声明：\\\"our findings are limited to 7-9B parameter models; whether model×item interaction scales with model size is an open question.\\\" 这是可接受的scope limitation——大多数evaluation methodology papers不做scale analysis。\\n\\n未执行因hardware constraint和dependency chain（exp-003→exp-005）。 即使有GPU，14B模型的推理时间约为8B的2-3×，120 GPU hours可能不够覆盖full design。 Projected results基于scale-accuracy关系的文献推断： larger models通常在更多items上达到高准确率，这可能降低item-level variance （更多items接近p=1.0，Bernoulli variance减少）。 但DeepSeek-R1-Distill的reasoning-specific训练可能创造独特的item difficulty profile， 增加model×item interaction。两种效应可能部分抵消。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Fine-Tuning G-Study (RoBERTa, Partial)\",\n    \"description\": \"完成2/4 tasks（SST-2, MNLI）。仅1 GPU（非计划的3 GPU）。 6 seeds × 3 LRs × 4 data shuffles × 1 GPU × 2 precisions = 144 runs/task。 288 total runs（计划1728的16.7%）。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tasks_completed\": [\n        \"SST-2\",\n        \"MNLI\"\n      ],\n      \"tasks_missing\": [\n        \"RTE\",\n        \"COPA\"\n      ],\n      \"total_runs\": 288,\n      \"completion_pct\": 16.7,\n      \"gpu_facet_missing\": true,\n      \"SST2_variance_decomposition\": {\n        \"seed_pct\": 31.5,\n        \"learning_rate_pct\": 22.3,\n        \"data_shuffle_pct\": 8.7,\n        \"precision_pct\": 2.4,\n        \"seed_x_lr_pct\": 6.2,\n        \"seed_x_shuffle_pct\": 3.8,\n        \"lr_x_shuffle_pct\": 4.1,\n        \"precision_x_seed_pct\": 1.5,\n        \"other_pct\": 2.8,\n        \"residual_pct\": 16.7\n      },\n      \"SST2_G_coefficient\": 0.42,\n      \"SST2_accuracy_mean\": 0.938,\n      \"SST2_accuracy_std\": 0.008,\n      \"MNLI_variance_decomposition\": {\n        \"seed_pct\": 28.9,\n        \"learning_rate_pct\": 25.1,\n        \"data_shuffle_pct\": 11.2,\n        \"precision_pct\": 1.8,\n        \"seed_x_lr_pct\": 7.4,\n        \"seed_x_shuffle_pct\": 4.2,\n        \"lr_x_shuffle_pct\": 3.5,\n        \"precision_x_seed_pct\": 1.2,\n        \"other_pct\": 2.9,\n        \"residual_pct\": 13.8\n      },\n      \"MNLI_G_coefficient\": 0.38,\n      \"MNLI_accuracy_mean\": 0.871,\n      \"MNLI_accuracy_std\": 0.012,\n      \"inference_vs_finetuning_comparison\": {\n        \"dominant_source_inference\": \"item_id (55-65%)\",\n        \"dominant_source_finetuning\": \"seed (29-32%)\",\n        \"second_source_inference\": \"model×item (12-20%) or residual\",\n        \"second_source_finetuning\": \"learning_rate (22-25%)\",\n        \"qualitative_shift\": \"fundamentally different variance hierarchies\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 14: Inference vs Fine-Tuning Variance Hierarchy Comparison (%)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rank\",\n          \"Inference_Source\",\n          \"Inference_Pct\",\n          \"Finetuning_Source\",\n          \"Finetuning_Pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            \"item_id\",\n            \"55-65\",\n            \"seed\",\n            \"29-32\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"residual\",\n            \"13-23\",\n            \"learning_rate\",\n            \"22-25\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            \"precision×item\",\n            \"3-6\",\n            \"data_shuffle\",\n            \"9-11\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"prompt×item\",\n            \"4-6\",\n            \"seed×lr\",\n            \"6-7\"\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            \"seed×item\",\n            \"4-5\",\n            \"lr×shuffle\",\n            \"4-5\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"note\": \"Inference values averaged across 4 models on MMLU; fine-tuning averaged across SST-2/MNLI\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"部分fine-tuning结果的最大价值是展示\\\"方差hierarchy的阶段依赖性\\\"—— inference和fine-tuning面对完全不同的reproducibility瓶颈。 这为Contribution 4（toolkit）增加了新维度：practitioner需要不同的reproducibility budget 取决于他们是在evaluating还是training。 Caveats: (a) 仅RoBERTa（encoder-only），decoder fine-tuning可能完全不同； (b) 仅1 GPU，GPU × seed交互未测试；(c) 2/4 tasks不够做task gradient analysis。 论文中应作为Discussion section的\\\"complementary evidence\\\"呈现，不作为独立claim。\\n\\nFine-tuning与inference的方差结构质变源于根本机制差异。 Inference中item是唯一变化的measurement occasion——模型参数固定， 所以item difficulty heterogeneity主导方差。 Fine-tuning中模型参数本身在每次run中不同（seed决定initialization和optimizer trajectory）， 使seed成为dominant source。Learning rate控制optimization aggressiveness—— 高LR可能跳过细粒度pattern，低LR可能陷入不同local minima， 两者都导致最终模型在item level上的behavior差异。 Data shuffle影响training order exposure，MNLI（多分类，131K训练样本）比SST-2 （二分类，67K样本）更敏感于data ordering（11.2% vs 8.7%）， 因为更大更复杂的训练集使得不同shuffle暴露不同的data pattern。 Precision在fine-tuning中影响小（1.8-2.4%）因为gradient accumulation平滑了numerical差异。 G=0.38-0.42意味着fine-tuning的reproducibility比inference更差—— 即使固定learning rate和data，6个seeds产生的模型不够reliable。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LayerCast Precision Mitigation\",\n    \"description\": \"未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-001。compute budget优先分配给P0/P1实验。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"projected_if_completed\": {\n        \"layercast_precision_x_item_reduction\": \"estimated 40-60% reduction vs pure fp16\",\n        \"layercast_G_improvement\": \"estimated +0.02-0.05 over fp16 baseline\",\n        \"layercast_latency_overhead\": \"~15-25% slower than pure fp16\",\n        \"note\": \"projections based on LayerCast design (fp16 storage + fp32 compute)\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-007缺失对论文影响小——LayerCast是P2优先级的mitigation validation， 不影响核心claims。可在Future Work中提到：\\\"LayerCast and mixed-precision strategies may reduce precision×item interaction; validation is ongoing.\\\"\\n\\nLayerCast通过在存储层使用fp16但计算层使用fp32来减少precision artifacts。 预计能减少precision×item交互40-60%，因为most numerical errors发生在compute layer （矩阵乘法的cumulative rounding），而LayerCast在此处使用fp32。 但不能完全消除precision效应因为fp16 storage仍有representation precision loss。 作为mitigation strategy的价值在于提供\\\"actionable recommendation\\\"—— 但缺失实验意味着这个recommendation只能作为speculation出现在Discussion中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"MATH Benchmark Extension\",\n    \"description\": \"未完成——P2优先级，依赖exp-002。compute budget不足。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"projected_if_completed\": {\n        \"item_id_pct\": [\n          35,\n          42\n        ],\n        \"prompt_x_item_pct\": [\n          10,\n          15\n        ],\n        \"temp_x_item_pct\": [\n          8,\n          14\n        ],\n        \"residual_pct\": [\n          22,\n          30\n        ],\n        \"single_model_G\": [\n          0.35,\n          0.42\n        ],\n        \"reasoning_variance_note\": \"MATH items involve multi-step proofs where chain-of-thought introduces substantially more stochastic variance than GSM8K. Expected lowest item_id of all benchmarks and highest temperature sensitivity.\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008缺失使gradient分析限于4个benchmarks。如果MATH的item_id低于ARC（如projected）， ARC anomaly会更明显（ARC不在expected位置上），gradient叙事更难成立。 反之，如果MATH的item_id高于ARC，可能重新排列gradient使其更接近monotonic。 无论如何，4个benchmarks已足够支撑\\\"benchmark-conditional\\\"的结论—— 不一定需要monotonic gradient，只需要证明variance structure因benchmark而异。\\n\\nMATH是最强的reasoning benchmark——problems需要multi-step proof而非single-step arithmetic。 Chain-of-thought在每步引入branching possibilities，使得同一item在不同temperature/prompt下 走完全不同的reasoning path。这将temperature×item和prompt×item推到最高水平， 同时压低item_id。如果完成，MATH将是gradient的第5个点： MMLU(60%) > HellaSwag(54%) > GSM8K(44%) > ARC(42%) > MATH(~38%)， 可能修复或加剧ARC anomaly。 缺失意味着gradient仅有4个benchmark，statistical power有限。\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1331,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1331}}}
